Experiment blocks as amended. Because the effective delay is $k=\ell+1$, the reporting lags $\ell=0,\dots,6$ used in B2 correspond to effective delays $k=1,\dots,7$; the theoretical no-delay case is not attainable and is not represented. Replication is twenty seeds per cell in B2, B4 and B5 and ten seeds per cell in B3 and B6. The standard scenario is $T=80$ quarters with thirty burn-in periods discarded, a capacity shock applied at period forty and lasting eight quarters, an initial stock ratio of 0.10 and a shock size of 0.50. The run total is the product of the declared factors; the block manifest, not this table, is the authority on the final count. Sources: the pre-registration and `docs/AMENDMENTS.md`.
